<description>&lt;p&gt;Thai forces are confronting renewed violence in Narathiwat, where surveillance cameras were torched and tyres set alight, and attacks continue across three southern provinces. The Thai foreign minister met Myanmar leader Min Aung Hlaing to discuss border security and arsenic-tainted rivers, while Thailand is demanding action on mining waste flowing from Myanmar. Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet used the Francophonie summit to accuse Thailand of occupying Cambodian land and called for resumption of border demarcation, prompting Thai army accusations that Cambodia is politicising a border temple display. The conflict recorded 35 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scmp.com/week-asia/economics/article/3374464/malaysian-plan-let-refugees-work-spurs-advocates-call-safeguards&quot;&gt;South China Morning Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxQSkZ6ZDRsRHdCWS1tekxiRWVocHExTGNRamhiYWVNQkFtWjZRRmxCQWdiVzBFblRnZU9xb2hTa0R6UWRtM05RUS14VHgybDdRaGdLS2JjaGtIVjVNOVhGNWIzNlFaVllhMm1Vc1JwX3E1c1dUTEV4VkxoODdidHV3SUxFTG1FeUtBV0UwVktWYlc2UmlfX1JUNHFCdUh1dExiYXJjQ2hOMXdGeU9Ed3hXSWhWOVk?oc=5&quot;&gt;Cambodianess&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxOZWd6bUo2VFBZeFFtSFE3bmpNN1hUM0c1bUFjSkZkVU10S1hGUTRvRVFub1QtY2l6NTRGYWM0dnpNUEFWR0pZakllQVVLaVdlY05aLV94MlFhcHpKOVNtWFdWdkN5Y1BQNlZfaHlqQ25PMnFfMk9hTXRyRERJTjVjV0xTbWRfcFBWZUs5V3pZRUxiZm5qNVp4VVlUZmF2STJFMWpKWEVGLXhPRlVvQnN3eXFCLVp3NVFkdUE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Khmer Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiAFBVV95cUxQdjR0UzNlbHJ3ajR1ektPblFSY1NFNVlkOHl0Tjl2TzNmcWpOdUdNanFuQzJ5VzNkdmlsVlZ4SlpWMDVmT3F4LTNQakRPNnM1Z0FqenpWODdWb3Jna3YyejZBNUlBSHVIQ2ZuSld4NlFHWmFkOTh0WFBKVWNlRmV5N0czcVZuWFlG?oc=5&quot;&gt;Taarifa Rwanda&lt;/a&g